 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1124) '| A README is 40 lines or fewer | 108 of 116 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1124) '**Rescinded: a README names its `DETAILS.md`.** The gate held this rule at 87 of 89 and then stopped checking it. The site prints `DETAILS.md` on the same page as its README, so a reader no longer needs a pointer to find it. The row above stays as it was measured, next to what it retracts. `check-rfd-structure.py` accepts a `DETAILS.md` the README does not name, and its self-test says so.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-1124) 'Two of these need their exception stated, because the number above is not 116 and the rule still shipped.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-1124) '**A `## Decision` section.** The two without it are RFD66606-1074 and RFD66606-1078. Both carry `State: abandoned`, which means another repository now develops the RFD, and an abandoned RFD states only where it went. The gate requires a Decision unless the state is `abandoned`, and that holds at 116 of 116.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-1124) '**A retracted decision renames its own heading.** RFD66606-1067 heads its section "Decision, as published and now retracted". The gate matches a heading that starts with `Decision` and a comma, so a retraction in place does not have to hide behind the original title.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-1124) 'Measured and not gated
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-1124) '**A `## Problem` section.** 111 of 116. The five without one are RFD66606-1000, RFD66606-1012, RFD66606-1015, RFD66606-1074 and RFD66606-1078. Four are abandoned, and RFD66606-1000 is the conventions document itself. The carve-outs would outnumber the signal, so the gate checks the position of Problem and not its presence.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-1124) '**A `## Related` section.** 111 of 116. RFD66606-1020, RFD66606-1021, RFD66606-1022 and RFD66606-1023 end at their Decision, and RFD66606-1074 has no section at all. The four look like omissions rather than a choice, and adding a section to somebody else's RFD is an edit this work did not make.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-1124) 'The line limit, and the two things it turned up
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-1124) 'RFD66606-1000 stated "under 40 lines" and 8 of 116 READMEs exceeded it, at 41, 43, 46, 82, 93, 131, 152 and 179 lines. Five were long because they carried a retraction in place, which `CLAUDE.md` requires, and that read as a conflict between two house rules.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-1124) 'It was not one. A retraction stays next to what it retracts, and after a move the thing it retracts is the detail, which lives in `DETAILS.md`. So the retraction goes there too and the rule is unbroken. All eight READMEs were split on that reading, and no retraction was deleted.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-1124) 'Splitting them turned up the second thing. With the eight fixed, **12 READMEs sat at exactly 40 lines**. Twelve files landing on one number is not chance, so the bound the corpus keeps is inclusive and RFD66606-1000's "under 40" was off by one. The document was corrected to "40 lines or fewer" and the gate reads the number from that sentence.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-1124) 'Three of the eight needed real compression rather than a move: RFD66606-1121, RFD66606-1122 and RFD66606-1123 state a long decision, and their READMEs went from 131, 152 and 182 lines to 39 each. Nothing was dropped. Every removed section either moved into `DETAILS.md` or was already there in fuller form, which is why three of them could go without a replacement.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-1124) 'The defects the measurement found, and the repairs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-1124) '- Citations in the old decimal form: count 37 in 32 files; repair Rewritten from the ALIASES.md map. The substitution keeps the same four characters, so every line wrap is unchanged.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-1124) '- `State: pre-discussion`: count 1, RFD66606-1064; repair Corrected to `prediscussion`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-1124) '- A state RFD66606-1000 does not list: count 2, RFD66606-1074 and RFD66606-1078; repair `moved` added to RFD66606-1000, because the use predates the list. The state left the list again when the vocabulary returned to the six, and both now read `abandoned`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-1124) '- A `DETAILS.md` no README named: count 2, RFD66606-1118 and RFD66606-1123; repair A pointer line added before Related, where the other 87 put it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-1124) '- A `DETAILS.md` with a title of its own: count 1, RFD66606-1000; repair Retitled `RFD 1000 details: numbering`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-1124) '- READMEs over the line limit: count 8 of 116; repair Split into `README.md` and `DETAILS.md`, retractions included.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-1124) '- RFD66606-1000's limit was off by one: count 1; repair Corrected to "40 lines or fewer", which is what 12 READMEs already sit on.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-1124) '- A heading written twice on one line: count 1, RFD66606-1122's `DETAILS.md`; repair `## What exists, and what does not## What exists, and what does not`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-1124) '- An RFD after the migration cannot pass: count latent; repair See below.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-1124) 'The last one had not fired yet. `check-rfd-numbers.py` required an ALIASES.md row for every directory. ALIASES.md maps an old number to a new one, and an RFD written after the migration has no old number. This RFD is the first such RFD, and it would have failed the gate that records how it is numbered. The check now reads the migrated range out of the table and applies only inside it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-1124) 'Why an AST, in a repository that had no dependency
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-1124) 'The gap is measurable rather than theoretical. The byte scan found 3 of the 37 unmigrated citations. The other 34 sat across a line break, and `RFD` on one line with `0019` on the next is two unrelated tokens to a regular expression and one citation to a reader.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-1124) 'Widening the expression to allow a newline would repair that one case. It would not repair the next one, because the class of defect is reading markup as text. The AST is where the distinction lives, and every later rule here reuses it: the metadata fields come from the strong-emphasis tokens rather than from counting asterisks, and the section spine comes from heading tokens rather than from lines that start with a hash.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-1124) '`markdown-it-py` is pinned in `scripts/requirements.txt`. A parser change would move what the gate sees, and a gate that changes verdict without a diff is not a gate.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-1124) 'The negative controls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-1124) '`python scripts/check-rfd-structure.py --self-test` builds a small tree for each case and asserts the verdict. One case is a clean tree that must pass. Fifteen are known-bad trees that must fail:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-1124) '    title number disagrees with the directory
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-1124) '    the title is not the first block
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-1124) '    a second level-1 heading
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-1124) '    no metadata paragraph
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-1124) '    a state RFD 1000 does not list
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-1124) '    Scope written before Feature
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-1124) '    an unknown metadata field
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-1124) '    no Decision section
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-1124) '    Decision written before Problem
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-1124) '    a decimal citation split across a line break
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-1124) '    a citation that resolves nowhere
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-1124) '    a DETAILS.md titled for another RFD
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-1124) '    a README past the line limit RFD 1000 gives
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-1124) '`check-rfd-numbers.py` carries seven of its own, including the two that reject the withdrawn hex form: a hex directory name must fail, and so must a hex heading over a decimal directory.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-1124) 'Both self-tests run before the gate itself in `.github/workflows/checks.yml`, so each proves it can reject before it judges the repository.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-1124) 'What the decimal renumbering withdrew
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-1124) 'Every count above was measured against the corpus while RFD numbers were hexadecimal and `ALIASES.md` existed. RFD66606-1000 renumbered the corpus to decimal and deleted that table. The measurements stay as measured. Two of the rules they produced do not.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-1124) 'The row reading "Every citation resolves to a directory or an ALIASES.md row" now reads "to a serial the registers list", live or deleted. This gate reads the registers that `RFD.Register.from_journals/1` builds from the journals rather than parsing them a second way (operator, 2026-11-26), so the two cannot disagree about which numbers exist. That is the arrangement the state list and the line limit already use, one file further along.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-1124) 'An earlier draft of this paragraph said the gate parses the deleted numbers out of RFD66606-1070's prose. It did, for one commit, and the register replaced it. The paragraph is corrected rather than deleted because a document that states a rule the code does not implement is the failure this whole RFD was written against, and it happened here.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-1124) 'The row reading "No citation uses the old decimal form" now covers two withdrawn forms. A number beginning with 0 is the first. A serial carrying a letter is the second, and 131 RFDs wore it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-1124) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-1124) 'A measurement over all 116 found nine kinds of defect. The largest was 37 citations still in the old decimal form. The number gate looked for those and reported 3. An RFD wraps its prose at about 72 columns, so a citation splits across a line break, and a scan of the bytes cannot see it. That gate measured the file. The rule is about the sentence.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1124  1 LINE
 Text:Written
